# Authentication

This template does not ship auth. When you add it, honor the same construction and
layering rules as every other dependency. Sketches (JWT and session) live in
`README.md` (Authentication), `src/app/state/README.md`, and
`src/app/middlewares/README.md`.

Identity is request-scoped. A route `Depends` on claims or session info and passes
`user_id` (and other fields the use case needs) into the service **method**. Do not
put identity on a service `__init__`. Do not import `Request` in `services/`.

```python
# BAD - request identity on a process-wide service
class OrdersService:
    def __init__(self, session: SessionInfo) -> None: ...

# GOOD - pass fields into the method
async def list_for_user(self, user_id: str) -> list[Order]: ...
```

Construct verifiers, token or session clients, and auth services in `lifecycle/` only.
No module-level `HTTPBearer()`, security scheme, or client. Read headers on the
`Request` inside the `Depends` (same pattern as `X-Session-ID`).

The HTTP layer does not call `RedisClient`. A `SessionService` (injected like
`FeatureFlagService`) loads the session. `require_*` accessors live next to
`get_feature_flag_service` and call `get_app_services()`.

Probes and `GET /metrics` omit the auth `Depends`. If you later need a uniform
pre-route 401, register ASGI only in `_add_middlewares_in_order`, before
`CorrelationIdMiddleware`, exempt paths via `app_consts.py`, and talk to a
service — never a client.
